menu "Audio manager"

    config AUDIO_MANAGER_MANUAL_RECORD_MAX_SECONDS
        int "Maximum manual recording duration (seconds)"
        range 1 120
        default 30
        help
            Compile-time upper bound for audio_manager_start_recording().
            Manual capture stops when the application requests stop or this
            duration is reached, whichever happens first. The manager allocates
            one shared retained-recording PSRAM buffer large enough for the
            larger of this limit and the fixed record_duration_seconds value.

    config AUDIO_MANAGER_WAV_PREFETCH_SECONDS
        int "WAV prefetch block duration (seconds)"
        range 1 30
        default 10
        help
            Each logical WAV prefetch block holds this many seconds of the
            accepted PCM16 mono 16-kHz source. At the default, one block is
            320000 bytes and the two PSRAM ping-pong blocks use 640000 bytes
            only while a WAV is active. The SD reader still uses bounded 4 KiB
            raw reads. The I2S-owning manager consumes only a READY block and
            applies its fixed PCM16 full-scale-to-output-ceiling map during TX;
            no whole-file WAV scan or source-file modification is performed.

    config AUDIO_MANAGER_GOLDEN_STABILITY_MODE
        bool "Run the golden record/DSP/playback stability loop"
        default n
        help
            Legacy default-off regression safety net for the proven Phase 11.3
            record -> DSP -> recorded-playback engine. Keep this only when a
            direct engine-level regression is intentionally required.

            Normal hardware validation and soak should use the external/public-
            API stress task instead, because that path also exercises command
            arbitration, public state transitions, callbacks/status counters,
            cancellation ownership, WAV streaming, and cleanup exactly as an
            application would.

            Golden mode monopolizes the manager operation slot, therefore
            production record/playback/WAV public commands are rejected while
            it is enabled.

    config AUDIO_MANAGER_GOLDEN_STABILITY_RECORD_SECONDS
        int "Golden stability recording duration (seconds)"
        range 1 120
        default 60
        depends on AUDIO_MANAGER_GOLDEN_STABILITY_MODE
        help
            Number of 16 kHz PCM24 samples retained before each golden DSP and
            recorded-playback cycle. The historical stress configuration uses
            60 seconds, which reserves about 3.66 MiB of PSRAM for recording.
            Allocation still fails safely if the target does not have enough
            free PSRAM.

    config AUDIO_MANAGER_GOLDEN_STABILITY_TASK_PRIORITY
        int "Golden stability task priority"
        range 6 7
        default 6
        depends on AUDIO_MANAGER_GOLDEN_STABILITY_MODE
        help
            FreeRTOS priority for the legacy golden engine-level regression.
            The default is 6. Use 7 only after measuring GUI/network
            responsiveness on the target.

endmenu
